{
  "$comment": "Conformance vectors for the framed carrier, normative in kernel/specs/controller-protocol.md §3, whose §11 cites them. Every table here is normative. `frame` is the whole frame in lowercase hex; `meta` is the text of its meta region, which is the typed-frame JSON (durable-execution.md §6) of the envelope; `data` is the data region in hex, empty for a message frame. A reader MUST produce `meta` and `data` from `frame`, and `frame` from them. An `undecodable` row is a frame a reader refuses; `reason` says why, and the row pins the refusal rather than a code name — the carrier-neutral code for it is owed by the step that implements the ABI carrier (§3.5).",
  "frames": [
    {
      "name": "a request before any session exists",
      "class": "message",
      "meta": "{\"id\":0,\"payload\":{\"generation\":4,\"kernel\":{\"runtime\":{\"name\":\"rust\",\"version\":\"1.84.0\"},\"telo\":\"0.103.2\"}},\"session\":null,\"type\":\"Session.Hello\"}",
      "frame": "",
      "data": ""
    },
    {
      "name": "a response, carrying the requester's id and the same type",
      "class": "message",
      "meta": "{\"id\":0,\"payload\":{\"ok\":{\"controller\":{\"runtime\":{\"name\":\"node\",\"version\":\"24.11.1\"},\"telo\":\"0.103.2\"},\"generation\":4}},\"session\":null,\"type\":\"Session.Hello\"}",
      "frame": "",
      "data": ""
    },
    {
      "name": "a request the controller end minted, with an odd id",
      "class": "message",
      "meta": "{\"id\":1,\"payload\":{\"instance\":\"h1\",\"reason\":\"listening on 8080\"},\"session\":\"s1\",\"type\":\"Hold.Acquire\"}",
      "frame": "0000006b01000000667b226964223a312c227061796c6f6164223a7b22696e7374616e6365223a226831222c22726561736f6e223a226c697374656e696e67206f6e2038303830227d2c2273657373696f6e223a227331222c2274797065223a22486f6c642e41637175697265227d",
